---
import { DOCS } from '../constants/site.ts';

const bodyParagraph = 'text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed text-zinc-400';
---

<section
  id="how-it-works"
  aria-labelledby="how-heading"
  class="py-20 md:py-28 border-t border-zinc-800"
>
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
    <h2 id="how-heading" class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-8">How It Works</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-3 mb-8 text-zinc-400">
      <li>A pull request is opened, by a person or an AI agent.</li>
      <li>Arbiter reads the policy from your protected policy repository.</li>
      <li>
        Arbiter checks the evidence GitHub holds: who approved, and which checks
        passed.
      </li>
      <li>
        The <code>Arbiter / authorize</code> check allows, blocks or escalates the
        merge when GitHub requires it, and says what is missing.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <p class={bodyParagraph}>
        Policy evaluation is deterministic: there are no LLMs in the enforcement
        path.
      </p>
      <p class={bodyParagraph}>
        Each decision is recorded with the policy commit it used, the approvals and
        checks it counted, and its result.
      </p>
      <p class={bodyParagraph}>
        Set it up with the
        <a href={DOCS.admin} class="text-zinc-100 underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">administrator manual</a>
        and the
        <a href={DOCS.starter} class="text-zinc-100 underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">starter policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
